## Status: incomplete

I built and verified a large metatheory infrastructure in `/workspace/Task.v` (it currently compiles with `make`), including:

- mutual free-variable and substitution functions for `qua`/`typ`/`qtyp`/`exp`;
- local-closure (`lc_*`) predicates, opening identities, and closure/opening lemmas;
- fresh-substitution, self-substitution, and substitution/opening commutation lemmas at all four expression/type levels;
- environment relations (`env_rel`, insertion/removal/payload-change lemmas) with well-formedness weakening;
- well-formedness of environments and binding lookups (`wf_env_binds`, `wf_env_remove_typ`, …);
- well-formedness, reflexivity, and **transitivity of qualifier subtyping** (`subqual_wf`, `subqual_refl`, `subqual_trans`, including the hard join/meet/eval cases);
- well-formedness and reflexivity of `sub`/`subqtype`;
- preservation of `type`/`qtype`/`qual` under type and qualifier substitution.

## Main remaining obstruction

The proof is still missing the target declarations (`preservation`, `progress`). The central blocker is **transitivity of type subtyping (`sub_trans`/`subqtype_trans`)**. Unlike `subqual_trans`, this cannot be proven by a simple induction on one derivation:

- in the `sub_arrow` case, one argument-position composition needs transitivity with the first premise of the *first* derivation as the left side, while the result-position composition needs the symmetric use of the *second* derivation;
- the `sub_all`/`sub_qall` cases additionally require narrowing under a changed bound (`bind_sub`/`bind_qua` payload);
- a single structural induction cannot supply both orientations, and Coq rejects a naive mutual fixpoint because recursive calls would not be on the caller’s structural argument.

Resolving this needs a genuine well-founded recursion on pairs of derivations (e.g. an accessibility/subderivation relation on packed derivation proofs with a product order), which then also unlocks narrowing, typing weakening, the three typing substitution lemmas, the typing inversion lemmas, and finally preservation.

## Verification

`make` currently succeeds because the file contains the verified infrastructure only; the two required theorems are **not yet present/proved**, so the deliverable is not met. I did not use `Admitted`, `admit`, `Abort`, or any axioms.

